nd left White in front for the rest of the game."}, {"turn": 32, "text": "GPT-6.1 Sol's E7 lost only 1.5 points, its first calm move after a long run of costly ones. The lead moved from -12.0 to -10.4, and White's play on the upper side was mostly cheap from here on."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either called the go tools (play, choose_opponent), parsed the returned board into groups and liberties (the inspect10 function), flood-filled empty regions to count final area, or wrote the SGF, log and review files. None of it looped over candidate moves, ranked moves, or played any continuation forward, so each move was chosen by the player outside the code.", "stop": false}}